1
00:00:00,171 --> 00:00:01,232
Okay, welcome everybody.

2
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:02,974
This is the Medford Historical Commission.

3
00:00:03,034 --> 00:00:04,495
Today is Monday, June 13.

4
00:00:06,097 --> 00:00:09,480
And I will read our little statement here and then we will get going.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:18,688
Pursuant to Chapter 20 of the Acts of 2021, this meeting of the City of Medford Historical Commission will be conducted via remote means.

6
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:24,334
Members of the public who wish to access the meeting may do so by using the Zoom link provided for in the agenda.

7
00:00:24,934 --> 00:00:33,363
No in-person attendance of members of the public will be permitted and public participation in any public hearing during this meeting shall be by remote means only.

8
00:00:35,236 --> 00:00:36,758
We have a very full agenda.

9
00:00:36,778 --> 00:00:39,040
So we're going to try to move things along.

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:46,926
Up first we are going to have a preferably preserved hearing for 130 Boston Avenue.

11
00:00:46,946 --> 00:00:49,789
So just to remind folks how we got here.

12
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:56,635
Two months ago we received an application for a partial demolition at 130 Boston Avenue.

13
00:00:57,215 --> 00:01:01,500
Last month, the property was determined to be historically significant.

14
00:01:02,181 --> 00:01:04,123
And let me remind folks of what that means.

15
00:01:04,703 --> 00:01:12,231
That means that the property is importantly associated with one or more historic persons or events, or with the broad architectural, cultural,

16
00:01:12,728 --> 00:01:30,257
political, economic, or social history of the city or the Commonwealth, or it is historically or architecturally important in terms of period, style, method of building construction, or association with an important architect or builder, either by itself or in the context of a group of buildings.

17
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:35,639
So based on that definition, last month, the property was determined to be historically significant.

18
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,241
So tonight we are doing a

19
00:01:39,661 --> 00:01:40,902
Preferably preserved hearing.

20
00:01:41,382 --> 00:01:58,132
And what that means is that the designation preferably preserved means that the commission has determined that after an open public hearing that the demolition of the building under review would be detrimental to the architectural or historic history, excuse me historical heritage of the city of Medford.

21
00:01:58,892 --> 00:02:11,485
And lastly, we just like to remind folks that the Medford Historical Commission does not and will not consider the building's condition or any safety issues when determining whether a building is to be preferably preserved.

22
00:02:12,045 --> 00:02:14,327
Only the building commissioner can address these issues.

23
00:02:17,407 --> 00:02:31,330
So what we'll do here tonight is we will go around for the commissioners to speak with regards to this property, then we will let the property owner speak, and then we will take any public comments before we take a vote.

24
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:40,992
So from my commissioners, if anyone would like to make a motion, either way, I will start the discussions.

25
00:02:55,062 --> 00:02:55,763
We need a motion.

26
00:02:56,704 --> 00:03:02,430
Yes, I'd take a motion, please, to start whether to find for preferably preserved or not.

27
00:03:07,336 --> 00:03:10,460
Make a motion to find 130 Boston Ave preferably preserved.

28
00:03:11,901 --> 00:03:12,522
Thank you, Ryan.

29
00:03:15,295 --> 00:03:15,615
Second.

30
00:03:16,256 --> 00:03:16,917
Thank you, Jess.

31
00:03:17,979 --> 00:03:21,324
Okay, Ryan, I'm going to start with you and then I'm going to go around.

32
00:03:21,884 --> 00:03:25,470
As I see folks on my screen, and then we'll go from there.

33
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:27,372
So Ryan you can start the discussion.

34
00:03:31,687 --> 00:03:48,756
at this building and I really think that in the context of the group of buildings that it's in, those are the five buildings or six buildings along Boston Ave from 124 to 138 Boston Ave.

35
00:03:49,737 --> 00:03:53,399
This is a really well preserved collection of Moses Mann buildings.

36
00:03:53,499 --> 00:03:57,301
Moses Mann was an important West Medford architect who

37
00:03:58,001 --> 00:04:02,325
really developed his own style, especially during the height of the Victorian era.

38
00:04:03,125 --> 00:04:09,310
And this is a beautiful example, even though it needs work, it's a beautiful example of Queen Anne architecture.

39
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:18,978
And it's a perfect representation of the types of works that he would do, not just here, but in the entire Smith estate.

40
00:04:19,238 --> 00:04:19,778
development.

41
00:04:19,978 --> 00:04:21,459
He had a role in there.

42
00:04:21,499 --> 00:04:23,560
He was basically the on the boots developer.

43
00:04:24,261 --> 00:04:30,664
He lived two doors up his workshop where he created all the woodwork for all these things was two doors down.

44
00:04:31,184 --> 00:04:43,110
So, you know, I think it's important to make sure that we preserve the integrity of these buildings and therefore I am very much in favor of finding for preferably preserved status for this building.

45
00:04:45,811 --> 00:04:46,832
Okay, thank you, Ryan.

46
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:49,277
Jess, I'll come to you next.

47
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,681
Yeah, I agree with everything that my fellow Commissioner said.

48
00:04:53,701 --> 00:05:11,054
I think the form B was really clear about the architectural value of the property and it just seems like this would be a really great opportunity to try to have some of that restored back to its former glory.

49
00:05:11,174 --> 00:05:14,577
So I agree with Ryan on that.

50
00:05:14,637 --> 00:05:14,937
Thanks.

51
00:05:15,817 --> 00:05:16,318
Thanks, Jess.

