840
01:00:17,671 --> 01:00:19,493
So they weren't sure if they're going to be able to make it.

841
01:00:19,674 --> 01:00:21,816
Are you talking about the property owners or the district?

842
01:00:21,896 --> 01:00:23,438
I am talking about the property owners.

843
01:00:23,698 --> 01:00:23,978
Okay.

844
01:00:24,018 --> 01:00:24,979
Thank you for clarifying.

845
01:00:25,080 --> 01:00:26,061
Go ahead.

846
01:00:26,081 --> 01:00:26,621
Sorry about that.

847
01:00:26,761 --> 01:00:32,928
And the architect was maybe thinking of coming, but I don't see his name there either.

848
01:00:32,988 --> 01:00:33,609
So, okay.

849
01:00:34,564 --> 01:00:47,230
At any rate, if you've read the emails and stuff, the homeowner really wasn't in favor of creating a local historic, single family local historic district.

850
01:00:47,310 --> 01:00:54,993
So I think that kind of speaks for itself.

851
01:00:56,614 --> 01:01:01,216
And I personally, as a commissioner, wasn't really in favor of it.

852
01:01:04,032 --> 01:01:06,333
Especially since the homeowner didn't want to do it.

853
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:11,716
So I think it would be a tough sell to the city.

854
01:01:12,037 --> 01:01:30,127
And I feel that since we've been working with the homeowner and the architect, they have revised their design to something that I feel is quite appropriate and doesn't change the overall massing of the house.

855
01:01:32,773 --> 01:01:36,456
It's essentially putting a porch on the back and dormers on the front and back.

856
01:01:36,696 --> 01:01:42,421
So, and we did go through a few iterations with them on the design.

857
01:01:43,643 --> 01:01:53,031
And so I know there was another additional letter written by one of the neighbors.

858
01:01:55,406 --> 01:02:04,750
Yes, and just for my commissioners, we did receive two public comments on the last 30 days about this property and both of those letters are in the Google Drive.

859
01:02:06,391 --> 01:02:07,771
If people would like to read them.

860
01:02:07,791 --> 01:02:10,973
I'm sorry, Peter, go ahead.

861
01:02:11,493 --> 01:02:20,157
One of them from Marianne there was, her comments were mostly about,

862
01:02:23,472 --> 01:02:30,037
Changing, we had some paired windows on the dormers, and she wanted to change those to single windows.

863
01:02:30,317 --> 01:02:36,662
So I don't know if they're willing to entertain that when I say they, the homeowners.

864
01:02:39,104 --> 01:02:44,908
And I believe one of the historic district commissioners also wrote a public comment, Frederick.

865
01:02:45,188 --> 01:02:46,009
He did, yes.

866
01:02:46,790 --> 01:02:48,511
And he had very few comments.

867
01:02:50,590 --> 01:02:56,194
Like additional comments, I think that he had one comment about making the front center windows smaller.

868
01:02:58,436 --> 01:03:11,305
Other than that, I think he felt that we did a decent job of working with them and trying to get something appropriate.

869
01:03:13,014 --> 01:03:18,760
I just would like to say, Peter, I got a message in the chat that the architect is here for seven.

870
01:03:19,400 --> 01:03:22,684
Yes, his name is not here, but he is here.

871
01:03:23,745 --> 01:03:28,449
So if we have questions or if there's additional comments, somebody is here representing the property owner.

872
01:03:28,469 --> 01:03:29,390
Okay.

873
01:03:33,850 --> 01:03:49,363
I would like to hear from all the commissioners on this because I think it's important to note for the record kind of how we fall with regards to a local historic district here before we talk about releasing the demo delay.

874
01:03:49,383 --> 01:03:54,928
I want to make sure that everybody has their say and has their thoughts out there.

875
01:03:55,168 --> 01:03:56,449
And from my understanding,

876
01:03:57,290 --> 01:04:00,351
historic district commission did talk about this at their last meeting.

877
01:04:00,391 --> 01:04:03,272
And as you said, Peter, the homeowners don't want it.

878
01:04:03,292 --> 01:04:06,293
I think it seemed a little mixed from the neighbors.

879
01:04:06,353 --> 01:04:09,774
I think the majority of people didn't want it, but there were a couple of neighbors that did.

880
01:04:10,495 --> 01:04:25,100
So, um, I know we kind of talked anecdotally, maybe two meetings ago about this, but I would like to just have my commissioners, you know, uh, state their position on this so that we have it for the record.

881
01:04:26,092 --> 01:04:27,693
So Jess, I'm going to ask you to start.

882
01:04:27,713 --> 01:04:33,078
I don't really think that we should be creating one home historic district.

883
01:04:33,098 --> 01:04:34,079
That's the proposal, right?

884
01:04:34,119 --> 01:04:36,601
That just this one property would be the historic district?

885
01:04:37,022 --> 01:04:37,442
Correct.

886
01:04:39,364 --> 01:04:43,307
So I am not in favor of that proposal.

887
01:04:44,148 --> 01:04:44,868
Thank you, Jess.

888
01:04:45,689 --> 01:04:46,069
Peter?

889
01:04:46,089 --> 01:04:49,633
I would agree with that in this case.

890
01:04:53,248 --> 01:05:13,812
Now, I'm aware that there are other homes where the homeowner does want to create a single-family historic district, and I guess I'm okay with that, you know, if that's what they want to do, and they view that as their legacy, so I don't mind them pursuing that.

891
01:05:15,753 --> 01:05:20,694
But in this case, since the owner was against it, and I didn't see that...

892
01:05:22,169 --> 01:05:31,437
how the home was being altered was detrimental to the integrity of the town or anything.

893
01:05:31,537 --> 01:05:40,444
So in my opinion, but so I was not in favor of it, of a single family local historic district.

894
01:05:41,945 --> 01:05:42,806
Okay, thank you, Peter.

895
01:05:42,826 --> 01:05:42,866
Ed.

896
01:05:44,908 --> 01:05:53,492
Again, I am highly skeptical of how you could have a district with one property in it, whether or not the homeowner agrees.

897
01:05:54,153 --> 01:06:04,497
There may be situations where that's appropriate, but I can't speak to this one, but this is one where I would generally be pretty skeptical.

898
01:06:07,099 --> 01:06:07,639
Thank you, Ed.

899
01:06:07,759 --> 01:06:08,059
Doug?

900
01:06:09,780 --> 01:06:13,882
Yeah, I mean, I obviously was close to this because I sit on the subcommittee with

901
01:06:14,363 --> 01:06:20,584
Peter and Ryan, we had multiple design meetings, got a lot of iterations.

902
01:06:20,664 --> 01:06:24,185
Peter did a lot of hand sketching, trying to come up with ideas.

903
01:06:24,285 --> 01:06:33,986
This was a very iterative process and the owners were very patient with us and we appreciated their patience because it's an important building.

904
01:06:34,066 --> 01:06:38,567
But I believe that almost every historic building needs to adapt and grow.

905
01:06:38,587 --> 01:06:43,288
And sometimes it's not just within the four walls, but sometimes it needs to go beyond the four walls to be functional.

906
01:06:44,067 --> 01:06:52,851
And I felt that this was a reasonable alteration to a significant historic house that we found significant and perfectly preserved.

907
01:06:52,871 --> 01:06:55,733
But that doesn't mean it's unchanged throughout time.

908
01:06:55,773 --> 01:06:56,973
It just doesn't work that way.

909
01:06:56,993 --> 01:06:58,734
And I don't think it should.

910
01:06:58,834 --> 01:07:08,159
I actually disagree with a few of my commissioners, because I think what I've seen over time is that getting historic districts passed is like an act of Congress.

911
01:07:08,179 --> 01:07:12,101
And if you know Congress, we haven't done much of anything in the last decade plus.

912
01:07:13,314 --> 01:07:21,301
I know that someone like Somerville has moved quickly and they have like, I think, 20 or 30 properties as single homeless star districts because they want to just protect the most important houses.

913
01:07:21,401 --> 01:07:27,606
So if you can work with the owners, it's not a bad thing to do, but we haven't done it much here.

914
01:07:27,706 --> 01:07:34,652
So it's, the jury is still out, but I don't, I never want to impose a district on an owner who's not willing to work with us on that.

915
01:07:34,672 --> 01:07:39,435
That doesn't seem fair as a homeowner myself, I would not want that to happen to me.

916
01:07:39,596 --> 01:07:42,338
So I think this is a reasonable design

917
01:07:42,965 --> 01:07:44,886
And we took our time making it right.

918
01:07:44,946 --> 01:07:46,766
And I think it's well done.

919
01:07:48,887 --> 01:07:49,527
Thank you, Doug.

920
01:07:50,488 --> 01:07:54,149
Ryan, I would just like to have you wrap up this agenda item.

921
01:07:54,269 --> 01:07:58,170
Yeah, I just I'm not in favor of a district here.

922
01:07:58,250 --> 01:08:05,313
I think there are times building might be fully demolished and threatened and it's

923
01:08:06,052 --> 01:08:14,939
gone forever, or there's times where a building might be gutted beyond recognition and all integrity stripped down bare to its bones.

924
01:08:15,880 --> 01:08:24,146
But in this particular case, I think the particular alteration, as Doug said, follows the natural progression of what's going to happen to a building.

925
01:08:24,166 --> 01:08:33,533
You can't, you certainly can't let nothing happen to a building unless, you know, it's the houses are not necessarily museums, they're living entities, they change with the times, they change with

926
01:08:33,933 --> 01:08:37,075
styles and they change with our methods of living.

927
01:08:37,235 --> 01:08:47,601
So I think it's important to acknowledge that the homeowners have worked with us to do what we asked in the demo delay, which is to mitigate the demolition.

928
01:08:47,721 --> 01:08:51,143
So I think it's partially successful in that regard.

929
01:08:51,203 --> 01:08:57,927
So I think I'm in favor of moving this process along, but I'm not in favor of a district.

930
01:09:00,889 --> 01:09:02,250
Okay, Ryan, thank you very much.

931
01:09:03,832 --> 01:09:06,093
